BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Step: 4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Title: Place equipment to the report and document everything) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Action: Match dehu and air-mover counts to the program report and log daily readings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Detail: Do not set 45 dehus and 75 fans in two rooms you will not get paid for. Document the reason for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (every repair step regardless of who the end user is [The DYOJO \(The DYOJO\) - onSDIprTeAU @ 00:48:01].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (Getting on a list is a sales campaign, not an application. Schoen's playbook starts with applying to every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (program, expecting to pay a fee, and accepting there is no guarantee of placement. The opening comes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (when an incumbent underperforms in a territory and the 'switch flips' [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:10:19]. The next) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (move is relationship work. Get the regional manager's name and number, introduce yourself, and invite them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (to walk your facility and inspect your equipment. In his words, it is 'very important to have the regional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (manager's name and number so you can introduce yourself' [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:11:42]. He also works the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (field side by having adjusters and agents push for the company. That push lands hardest when claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (volume is high and the program needs capacity [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:12:01]. David Smith's addition is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (commitment. Once inside, learn both the program requirements and the carrier requirements, because both) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (rule sets apply to the same file [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:12:23]. The sequence matters. Applications sit dormant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (until a slot opens. The regional manager decides who fills that slot, and adjuster and agent advocacy tips the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (decision. Whether a contractor stays on the list once the switch flips depends on mastering two rulebooks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (Inside the program, the drying math is dictated rather than negotiated. Schoen describes the 'micia' report,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (timestamped day by day, which sets dehumidifier and air-mover counts that can fall below S500. If the room) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (calls for a small dehu, you are paid for a small even if you placed a large [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:06:02]. David) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (Smith sees contractors overshoot in the other direction. They set '45 D HUs and 75 fans in two rooms' and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (then do not get paid for it [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:44:40]. The paperwork load is a fixed cost to plan for.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (Documentation must be uploaded twice, once to your own system and once to the program, though some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (CRMs auto-upload [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:05:23]. Xactimate is mandatory and a second software platform) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (may be required. Schoen tells owners to either train admin staff or sub the paperwork out [-0hAYhkhJaw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (00:06:42]. The practical read is direct. Set equipment to match what the program's report will pay. Log) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (readings daily to show specific humidity dropping, and keep estimating in Xactimate from the first visit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (forward. Shops that set equipment by feel end up arguing with a reviewer over gear they already paid to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (haul in, run and pull back out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (The economics reward speed and volume rather than per-job margin. Schoen describes somewhat regular) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (job flow through rotation, scored on arrival speed and direct customer reviews. He is blunt that you are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm ('going to pay 5 10% a fee to be on the program' [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:08:41]. He adds that mitigation pays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (well while construction is harder [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:09:17]. The program wars show what TPAs actually) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (sell to carriers. Alacrity won Nationwide by promising $5M a year in savings, with no roughly $100 setup fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (and no $150 service-call fee. Contractor Connection took the account back with a 3-day drying cap it pitched) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (as $20M in savings [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:03:50]. Each of those savings is a line the contractor no longer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (bills. Ty Penzone explains how repair shops still make the channel work: subs accept lower rates in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (exchange for year-round volume [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:55:23]. Put the numbers together and the model is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm (clear. Arrival speed and reviews win the rotation, and mitigation carries the margin while construction fights) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.22 Tm (the list. Every dollar a TPA promises a carrier comes out of fees and drying days the contractor used to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.00 Tm (control. The model only works when crews and subs stay busy enough to spread the fee across many files.) Tj ET
