0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (S500, so if the room calls for a small dehu you are paid for a small even when you placed a large) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm ([-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:06:02]. The caps come straight from TPA sales pitches to carriers: Alacrity won) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Nationwide by promising $5M a year in savings by dropping the roughly $100 setup fee and $150) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (service-call fee, and Contractor Connection won the account back with a three-day drying cap claiming) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm ($20M in savings [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:03:50]. David Smith sees contractors set '45 D HUs and 75 fans in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (two rooms' and then get nothing for it [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:44:40]. Schoen's readings rule closes the loop:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (the logs must show specific humidity dropping day over day [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:08:21]. Even when the file) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (is clean, Schoen warns payment is still not guaranteed, because a homeowner can walk away with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (money. The economics check is simple: run the job to the program's equipment math and drying window,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (not to your own habits, and log readings that prove every day billed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (The second trap is building a company whose survival depends on someone else's dispatch queue. Ty) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Penzone's flooring company ran 125 homes a year from 2002 to 2006 while charging retail clients 1.5 times,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (then fell to one job in a month in 2008 [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:56:46]. One DYOJO panelist puts it bluntly: 'I) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (had a business that its entire solvency was built around doing 150 jobs a year plus' [onSDIprTeAU @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (00:59:09], which is why Ty argues for running diversified models to survive a 'model interrupt.' Back-office) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (load is the quieter drain. Jon Schoen reports that documentation must be uploaded twice unless a CRM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (auto-uploads, that Xactimate is mandatory and a second software may be required, and that owners should) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (plan to train admin staff or sub the paperwork out [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:06:42]. Joe Boyle of ClearFile sees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (the same scheduling trap from the administrator's own licensing desk: approvals take one week to three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (months, renewals cluster January through March, and financials must be current within 30 to 60 days, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (step one is 'a very modest timeline' [kR0zavFV0HU @ 00:02:38]. Underestimating paperwork time, on either) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (side of the TPA relationship, quietly kills margin and deadlines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (The third trap is signing or working under paper nobody read. On Relentless Health Value, 32BJ's Claire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (Brockbank and host Stacey Richter peg about 95% of employers as deferring to the TPA's paper and losing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (rights in fine print like a 'footnote on page 78,' because 'very few of us have contracting expertise, so we) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (accept the language' [pNIYu-t990E @ 00:06:09]. The cost was concrete: upside-down claims ran 32BJ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (about $10M in one year, with a $100 bill paid at $200, and the typical failure has sales overpromising,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (lawyers retracting, and contracting still open a year into implementation [pNIYu-t990E @ 00:04:19]. Their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (rule after signing is 'You have to police this.' On the claims side, Leah Small of Chisholm Chisholm &) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (Kilpatrick reports that Sedgwick recommends approval or denial without paying benefits, often aims to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (minimize payouts, and leans on file reviews instead of exams so treating physicians get dismissed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm ([lnhw4pYCOFU @ 00:01:29]. The fatal mistake is a thin appeal: in most cases no new evidence is allowed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (after the appeal closes, so every denial basis has to be rebutted with vocational reports, symptom journals,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (and physician reports up front [lnhw4pYCOFU @ 00:02:54]. Whether the counterparty is a plan buyer or a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (claimant, losing the record early is losing the fight.) Tj ET
