BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm ([33iGNdZ6fyE @ 02:10:13]. Brendy Riley's field workflow at Octagon mirrors it: environmental controls first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (to stop soot and carcinogens resettling, then demo, media blasting depending on char level and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (clean-versus-replace call, then HEPA vacuum, chem sponge and damp wipe, odor mitigation throughout,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (and finally a fire and smoke sealer, where "usually it takes one to two applications to mitigate any lingering) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (odors" [WTz841eMFkk @ 00:04:03]. Travis Chauncey of Abbotts explains why the HEPA step is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (non-negotiable: smoke particulates run under 10 microns, so a regular shop vac will not capture them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm ([iiCSRcut-WA @ 00:01:33]. Annissa Coy carries that into contents, HEPA-vacuuming before boxing,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (especially under heavy soot, and unpacking only inside the processing center under a HEPA scrubber) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm ([MkCNqNRsk04 @ 00:01:37]. Chris puts it flatly elsewhere: the most effective removal is physical, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (hydroxy. The consensus baseline: physical removal first, deodorize second, seal last, on a clean, dry) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (surface as the sealer label itself requires.) Tj ET
BT /F0 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (Practitioner consensus on fire, smoke and contents documentation) Tj ET
