BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (working in the contractor's favor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Items: Never hand the adjuster your estimate at the meeting; tell them you were hired to perform all repairs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (they prescribe and you are there for your marching orders, so they show their cards first [Chad Michael -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (The Practitioner - DmesIP8hcak @ 00:39:21].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (When your number is far from theirs, send an Xactimate photo report with no line items instead of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (estimate; Chad's ran 172 pages with two photos each to force a reinspection aimed at full siding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (replacement [Chad Michael - The Practitioner - DmesIP8hcak @ 00:41:19].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Write the lender contract precisely, because a vague contract leaves the mortgage claim handler to interpret) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (what is owed and stalls the money in a communication breakdown [Richard Levisee - VFWDHse67ws @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (00:03:44].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Put the contract price on the insurance contract so it matches the price on the insurance claim estimate,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (letting that contract double as the contractor's estimate for the lender [Integrity Roofing and Painting -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Mi6XZq4h6yo @ 00:02:21].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (The sharpest split on this desk is what a contractor does about the homeowner's deductible. Anne Pullen) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (opens flat: a contractor offering to cover or waive the deductible is asking the homeowner to commit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (insurance fraud, and the usual method is inflating the estimate to absorb it [tLwSSUZ6Awc @ 00:00:00].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (Brent Simmons of Restoration Roofing calls waiving it 100 percent illegal, compares it to a doctor's copay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (nobody ever forgives, and warns that the missing $2,000 on a $20,000 roof comes out of roof quality) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm ([t6BiCluK7GY @ 00:01:46]. State Restoration Services sells the opposite outcome without the illegal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (method: the pitch is pulling enough money from the carrier that the homeowner pays absolutely nothing,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (which the speaker says works 99 percent of the time, while insisting it is not waiving the deductible and not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (cash back [06ChGuOZCto @ 00:01:16]. Chad Michael sits in the middle. Chad mocks the Facebook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (contractors who claim every client writes a deductible check, saying it just does not happen, and draws the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (felony line only at lying to the carrier about the billed amount [DmesIP8hcak @ 00:24:25]. Chad's legal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm (workaround is hunting non-recoverable ACV money, such as a fence the owner may never repair, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm (signing that separate check over toward the deductible, then telling the adjuster exactly what was done) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm ([DmesIP8hcak @ 00:27:37].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (Assignment of benefits splits the room by vantage point. Timothy Ankle of Butler Legal, counseling carriers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm (in Florida, lays out the contractor's logic: the executed AOB gives the contractor confidence of payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.02 Tm (because the claim goes straight to the insurer, and Florida law holds that a policy's anti-assignment clause) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 214.80 Tm (does not block post-loss assignment of benefits [rxahzd6qaCw @ 00:01:32]. Crossroads Insurance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.57 Tm (Recovery concedes AOB at first looked like a good idea after Hurricanes Florence and Michael, since) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.35 Tm (destroyed properties could not reliably receive mail or money, then reports contractors began walking off) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.12 Tm (half-started jobs or doing hasty shoddy work once the money was locked in [iKLGuESx4po @ 00:01:10].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 153.90 Tm (Holmes Drafting Services, speaking from the agency side, calls AOB a four-letter word and walks the worst) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.67 Tm (case: the roofer bills a $100,000 roof, the carrier values the shingle roof at $20,000, and the roofer liens the) Tj ET
